## Left Rotation Logic

A left rotation around node `x` looks like this:

Before:

```text
    x
     \
      y
     / \
    T2 T3
```

After:

```text
      y
     / \
    x  T3
     \
     T2
```

Algorithm:

```text
LEFT-ROTATE(T, x)
    y = x.right
    x.right = y.left

    if y.left != NIL
        y.left.parent = x

    y.parent = x.parent

    if x.parent == NIL
        T.root = y
    else if x == x.parent.left
        x.parent.left = y
    else
        x.parent.right = y

    y.left = x
    x.parent = y
```

Right rotation is symmetric.

---

## Insertion Algorithm

Insertion starts as a normal Binary Search Tree insertion.

```text
RB-INSERT(T, z)
    y = NIL
    x = T.root

    while x != NIL
        y = x
        if z.key < x.key
            x = x.left
        else
            x = x.right

    z.parent = y

    if y == NIL
        T.root = z
    else if z.key < y.key
        y.left = z
    else
        y.right = z

    z.left = NIL
    z.right = NIL
    z.color = RED

    INSERT-FIXUP(T, z)
```

---

## Insertion Fix-Up Cases

While the parent of `z` is red, there is a violation.

### Case 1: Uncle is red

Recolor:

```text
parent = BLACK
uncle = BLACK
grandparent = RED
z = grandparent
```

### Case 2: Uncle is black and node is an inner child

Rotate to convert to Case 3.

Example: `z` is right child of a left parent.

```text
z = parent
leftRotate(z)
```

### Case 3: Uncle is black and node is an outer child

Recolor and rotate around grandparent.

```text
parent = BLACK
grandparent = RED
rightRotate(grandparent)
```

Mirror the cases if the parent is the right child of the grandparent.

At the end:

```text
root.color = BLACK
```

---

## Deletion Algorithm

Deletion is harder because removing a black node may break the black-height property.

Main idea:

```text
RB-DELETE(T, z)
    y = z
    yOriginalColor = y.color

    if z.left == NIL
        x = z.right
        transplant(z, z.right)

    else if z.right == NIL
        x = z.left
        transplant(z, z.left)

    else
        y = minimum(z.right)
        yOriginalColor = y.color
        x = y.right

        if y.parent == z
            x.parent = y
        else
            transplant(y, y.right)
            y.right = z.right
            y.right.parent = y

        transplant(z, y)
        y.left = z.left
        y.left.parent = y
        y.color = z.color

    if yOriginalColor == BLACK
        DELETE-FIXUP(T, x)
```

---

## Deletion Fix-Up Cases

Deletion fix-up handles the situation where node `x` has an extra black.

Let `w` be the sibling of `x`.

---

### Case 1: Sibling is red

```text
w.color = BLACK
x.parent.color = RED
leftRotate(x.parent)
w = x.parent.right
```

This transforms the situation into one of the other cases.

---

### Case 2: Sibling is black and both sibling’s children are black

```text
w.color = RED
x = x.parent
```

The extra black moves upward.

---

### Case 3: Sibling is black, sibling’s near child is red, far child is black

```text
w.left.color = BLACK
w.color = RED
rightRotate(w)
w = x.parent.right
```

This converts to Case 4.

---

### Case 4: Sibling is black and sibling’s far child is red

```text
w.color = x.parent.color
x.parent.color = BLACK
w.right.color = BLACK
leftRotate(x.parent)
x = root
```

Again, mirror these cases if `x` is the right child.

At the end:

```text
x.color = BLACK
```

---

